gers.\n- **Line 16 & 17**: Always executed when ISR2 triggers.\n- **Line 23**: Condition can be satisfied if ISR1 and/or ISR2 run before ISR3.\n\n### Conclusion\nAll read/write operations related to `data` can be executed under certain conditions. The atomicity violation reported involves concurrent access patterns typical in ISR contexts, which are valid concerns but not false positives due to potential concurrent executions.\n\n### Final Report\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 17, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 17, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
